WEBVTT

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.200
<i>Oh Yeah!
tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.200
<i>Oh Yeah!
Be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:24.250
<i>oozora kidou wo koero</i>

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:24.250
<i>Pass the orbit beyond the sky</i>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:41.020
<i>osaekirenai maenomeri na speed</i>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:41.020
<i>Can't hold back this rushing speed</i>

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:46.020
<i>minareta machi ga diorama ni naru</i>

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:46.020
<i>A familiar town turns into a diorama</i>

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:51.230
<i>futoumei na sora tsukinukerunda</i>

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:51.230
<i>Burst through the unclear skies</i>

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.410
<i>nayami toka fuman toka futtobashite</i>

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.410
<i>Blow away your worries and discontent</i>

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:01.830
<i>manual doori no tabi nanka irane</i>

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:01.830
<i>Who needs a journey that's by the book</i>

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:07.620
<i>mayottemo furuetemo koudo agete</i>

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:07.620
<i>Even if you're lost or trembling,
Raise the altitude</i>

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.630
<i>Oh Yeah!
ikigatte shikujitte tachiagatte</i>

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.630
<i>Oh Yeah!
Show off, mess up, stand back up</i>

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.720
<i>kimi to mitsumeru michi naru chiheisen</i>

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.720
<i>The unknown horizon I watch with you</i>

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:22.600
<i>saa tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:22.600
<i>Now, be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:28.400
<i>asu wo terasu taiyou
mejirushi ni shitesa</i>

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:28.400
<i>Use the sun
That lights tomorrow as a guide</i>

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.230
<i>tonde ike jiyuu na Glorious World</i>

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.230
<i>Fly off to the Glorious World of freedom</i>

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:42.990
<i>After the final battle to decide
the Digital World's fate,</i>

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:48.420
<i>the Chosen Ones and their Digimon
succeeded in annihilating Millenniumon.</i>

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.920
Taichi, we did it!

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.960
So our mission is now over.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.850
Jeez, that just ruined the mood!

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.850
<i>Koshiro-kun!</i>

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.230
Gerbemon!

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.520
<i>Oh, it connected! It connected!</i>

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.820
Gerbemon...

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.490
Ah, the one Taichi mentioned before.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:22.000
Yeah, the Digimon I met
on the mountain of garbage.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.750
<i>Well, well, I haven't seen
clear skies like this in a while!</i>

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.670
What do you need?
We were in such a good mood.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.090
<i>Now, now!</i>

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:33.920
<i>Koshiro-kun...</i>

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.920
<i>you recognize this symbol, correct?</i>

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:38.930
Yes...

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:42.430
THE MYSTERY HIDDEN WITHIN THE CRESTS

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.930
Where are you right now?

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.440
<i>Now, don't be surprised!</i>

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:52.940
<i>After we left that mountain of treasure
for an explorative journey,</i>

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.520
<i>we reached...</i>

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:10.960
<i>A place where all kinds of information
in the Digital World is gathered!</i>

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.720
Hello? We're coming in...

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.570
Koshiro-kun!

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.740
Searchmon! Gerbemon!

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.460
Let me introduce you.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:54.170
This is the seeker of knowledge, Wisemon!

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:58.920
It's a pleasure to meet you,
Chosen Ones.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.920
WISEMON

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:03.010
This meeting brings great joy
to my knowledge.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:07.940
<i>What is the Digital World...
What are Digimon...</i>

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.480
Where do we come from
and where do we go...

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.940
We gather information and research daily.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:18.320
This brings joy to my knowledge.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.570
That's a lot of joy.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:24.370
So does that mean you love to study?

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:27.410
Joe, maybe you guys will get along.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.830
I don't know...

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.830
MECHANORIMON

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.580
BOKOMON

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.330
Now, come along, everyone.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:48.600
Wow... it's like a laboratory!

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.980
Digimon with high intellect, curiosity,
and a questioning mind

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:56.940
naturally come together
from all over the Digital World

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:00.070
and they share information and debate.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:05.330
At times, we carry out field studies
to look for answers.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.330
This is a facility for that!

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:11.750
Since I was invited here,
new discoveries have continued to be made.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:15.000
And it brings joy to my knowledge!

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.080
The joy is spreading.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:22.680
What's that?

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.260
Oh, that's garbage... ahem...

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:30.300
I mean, the place we store
unsortable damaged or corrupted data.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.770
It's like the inside of a computer.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:40.480
This enormous tree itself was discovered
by researchers many generations before us.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.610
There are many
historical artifacts stored here.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:50.120
We use this place as our base
as we conduct our research.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.890
Oh! Aren't those symbols...

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:17.020
Looks familiar... or actually,
we know them well, don't we?

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.520
It's the same ones that appear
on our Digivices.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.520
But how come?

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.990
The time when these shapes were born...

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:31.120
No matter how much we unravel history,
we cannot discover that answer.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.330
"Long ago."

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.790
So far into the past
that those words cannot describe it.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:41.300
You can say they existed
since the beginning of the world.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.800
There's no other conclusion.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:46.670
The greatest mystery to us...

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.630
<i>the crests.</i>

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.800
<i>That is what we call them.</i>

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:53.930
The crests...

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:58.680
It is said they are hidden codes
that structure all of the world.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:03.690
It is said they are messages sent
from somewhere else...

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:07.440
That they are records of all,
the answers to all.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:11.990
Our predecessors produced many theories,
challenging the mysteries,

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.950
but they never succeeded
in reaching the truth.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:17.750
However, one thing is clear...

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:25.210
These crests will play a key role
in avoiding the world's current anomalies.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:30.720
I do not know the reason why.
Something within us is telling us this.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.010
There's no other way to explain it.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.890
I've always wondered about it.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:42.730
Though I only thought of it as an icon
that indicates the Digivice's owner.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.690
There's more to this crest than that?

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.370
This must be...

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:59.630
The verification of the crests
and the Chosen Ones' data...

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.500
are matching and resonating!

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.460
The crests are likely reading them.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.180
The data of their adventure so far.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:13.800
Adventure...

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:17.640
Our experiences...

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.480
H-Huh?

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.330
What is it?

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:39.790
All of you and the crests
share a deep connection.

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.710
There is no question about that now.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.960
So let me state this.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:49.340
You children are the existence
who hold the Digital World's fate.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:52.470
The ones who summoned all of you here,

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:56.640
that would be us, Digimon,
as well as this Digital World itself.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:01.350
This truly brings joy to my knowledge!

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.600
That's quite a big story.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:08.030
So we were amazing!
Though we were a bit slow to realize.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:12.360
Well, in any case,
that new darkness thing is over anyway.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:13.860
No...

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.150
What?

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:19.960
You children are the only ones
who can defeat the Great Catastrophe

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.490
that is about to come.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.620
That is about to come?

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.120
The Great Catastrophe...

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:30.090
Wasn't that Millenniumon?

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:34.300
Millenniumon... in other words,
the uncontrollable darkness,

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.630
was only just a stepping stone.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:43.600
<i>You are aware that a large amount
of energy has been drawn</i>

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.600
<i>from the human world by some entity.</i>

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.740
<i>Even with Millenniumon gone now,</i>

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:52.070
this still has not stopped.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:55.200
That's what we learned from our research.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:59.370
The energy's destination
could not be traced even with our powers.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:03.700
To conclude,
that entity's will must be still alive.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:08.960
Something darker than Millenniumon
is about to make the move.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:12.630
Which means our role still continues.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:15.210
What happens in the Great Catastrophe?

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.050
All we know is this.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.350
It's completely blank.

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:21.730
Is it broken?

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:24.560
No, this is the answer.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:26.940
Huh? You mean...

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:28.440
We do not know...

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.730
is what we do know.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.530
This, too, brings joy to my knowledge.

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:35.990
What the heck? That's not funny!

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.990
How does that bring joy?!

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:26.490
Wisemon!

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:29.040
We're under attack!

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.790
There's a Digimon eating everything!

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.670
PUCCHIEMON

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:35.210
Even the data
on the Great Catastrophe.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.300
Nearly all of
the important data was eaten!

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:39.800
Impossible!

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.640
It's dangerous here too!

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:43.300
Evacuate now!

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:45.800
Who can it be?

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.440
What is that?

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:03.450
The most gluttonous Digimon
who eats any kind of data...

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.530
Burpmon!

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.450
BURPMON

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:14.830
Agumon!

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.800
Agumon Evolution!

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.340
Greymon!

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.350
How dare you try to steal important data?!

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:31.230
What a thief! Or rather a dine and dash?

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.480
Watch out!

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:37.070
Palmon Evolution!

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:38.190
Togemon!

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:40.950
Gabumon Evolution!

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:41.990
Garurumon!

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:44.620
Piyomon Evolution!

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:45.660
Birdramon!

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.410
Tentomon Evolution!

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:49.490
Kabuterimon!

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:52.080
Gomamon Evolution!

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.250
Ikkakumon!

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:57.880
Why?

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.880
Mega Flame!

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:05.760
Alright! We did it!

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:15.770
Fox Fire!

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:18.150
Meteor Wing!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.570
Harpoon Vulcan!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.360
Prickly Bang-Bang!

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:27.280
Mega Blaster!

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.660
That Digimon can eat all attacks?!

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.420
Burpmon got bigger again.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:43.920
How dare you?!
This calls for the last resort!

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:54.640
Hey! Whoa!

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.100
Gerbemon!

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.230
Oh, ow!

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:08.820
Seems like Burpmon has a preference.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.830
So much power...

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.130
No joke, seriously!

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.630
First, let's take this outside!

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:21.630
-Okay!
-Alright!

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:28.380
Greymon Super Evolution!

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:30.260
Metalgreymon!

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:33.520
Birdramon Super Evolution!

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:34.770
Garudamon!

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:45.280
Kabuterimon Super Evolution!

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.030
Atlurkabuterimon!

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.290
Giga Storm!

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:08.300
Burpmon's trying to get inside again!

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:10.810
So Burpmon's target is the data here?

00:15:10.810 --> 00:15:13.260
Shadow Wing!

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:22.570
What do we do
against an enemy that eats attacks?

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:25.610
Attacks... Eats data...

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:28.530
If we just had some bigger data...

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:31.110
<i>Big data...</i>

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.410
That's it!

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:34.580
Everybody!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.460
Flower Cannon!

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:48.840
Sorry for the wait!

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:51.800
The garbage data?

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:03.850
If you wanna eat that much,
have some of this!

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:25.000
If we can overload Burpmon's single intake
with a massive amount of data...

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:38.140
Horn Buster!

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:43.890
Giga Storm!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.530
We did it!

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.160
We managed to retrieve the data.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:08.130
But if they're all scattered like this,
restoring them will be grueling!

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:10.170
I'll help!

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:15.260
All the data was saved
thanks to you children.

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:18.300
This truly brings joy to my knowledge!

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:23.680
But that Great Catastrophe
is about to begin, right?

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:26.940
We still have business left to finish.

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:31.200
Just when I thought it was finally over.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:34.190
Jeez, how long is this gonna continue?!

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:39.070
We can still continue our adventure.

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:40.700
I'm gonna do it.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:44.340
If Agumon's with me,
I have nothing to fear!

00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:45.460
Yup!

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:50.590
Not because I was chosen
or because it's my mission.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:55.670
I like Agumon and everyone...
I do it because I like Digimon!

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:57.720
Taichi!

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:14.190
What's this?

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:16.330
What is it?

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:18.240
A new phenomenon!

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:22.540
Oh, another joy to my knowledge!

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:23.750
Huh?

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:26.540
The direction of the arrows are different.

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:28.670
They're all different.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.540
What does this mean?

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:36.100
The crests are the key
to avoiding the Great Catastrophe...

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:38.100
is what I explained earlier.

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:42.310
But in fact, we do not know
anything more than that.

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:47.360
You mean that answer lies
where these arrows point?

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:48.850
I believe so.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.150
Let's go, Taichi!

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:52.060
Yeah!

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:00.870
Hey, Taichi...

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:04.790
Hm? Hey, why only mine?

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:09.090
Well, we'll find out
when we get there, right?

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:10.040
Yeah!

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:14.550
I am sure there are many things
calling for you children.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:17.680
Please, find those answers for us.

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:23.980
Um, I think I'll stay here a little longer
to research something and then set out.

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:27.060
I want to help
with restoring the data too.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.060
Okay, gotcha.

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:31.940
Tailmon?

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:33.280
I'm fine.

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:34.570
But...

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:38.440
You couldn't evolve earlier,
so I'm worried.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.490
Maybe you're tired?

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:43.080
You did go through extreme evolutions.

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:45.960
Let's rest a little before we go.

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:47.540
Tailmon...

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:50.710
No, this is nothing.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:55.260
Fatigue, huh...
You need to relax when you're tired.

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:57.460
Relax, hmm...

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:03.800
The hot springs!

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:06.020
Hot springs?

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:10.230
We'll guide you there!
We're pretty familiar with the place.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.150
Let's go.

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:13.060
Yeah.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:14.770
But...

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:19.190
We want you
and Patamon both to get better.

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.200
Okay.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:26.200
Then Leader, Gomamon, please guide us.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:27.790
Alright!

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:30.700
Now, everyone, let's set out!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:53.810
Koshiro-kun, what's bothering you?

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:58.950
I'm wondering
if Burpmon only came to eat data.

00:20:58.950 --> 00:20:59.940
Hm.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:03.860
An attack just after
we closed in on the crest's mystery.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:08.080
There may be a connection
with the Great Catastrophe.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:12.080
A mystery leads to more mysteries.
This too...

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:14.710
Brings joy to my knowledge!

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.040
It really does!

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:20.340
I can't wait, Taichi!

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:23.600
Yeah, we're gonna find the answer!

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:25.590
The answer to the crests!

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:33.140
<i>ima mazari atteku border</i>

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:33.140
<i>The border has now begun to blend</i>

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.980
<i>koko kara wa jinrui mitou desu!</i>

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.980
<i>"It's uncharted territory from here!"</i>

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:38.520
<i>aoi sora umi no hate</i>

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:38.520
<i>Blue skies, the ends of the ocean</i>

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:42.610
<i>nozomu kagiri no subete ga aru kara</i>

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:42.610
<i>All that you desire awaits you</i>

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:55.870
<i>owari nanka nai ze sou sa</i>

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:55.870
<i>The end doesn't exist, that's right</i>

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.540
<i>koko wa ima bokura no shuppatsuten</i>

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.540
<i>We're at our starting point right now</i>

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:01.170
<i>aoi sora umi no hate</i>

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:01.170
<i>Blue skies, the ends of the ocean</i>

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:04.760
<i>dare mo shiranai asu wa aru kara</i>

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:04.760
<i>There's a tomorrow that no one knows about</i>

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:06.760
<i>waratte iyou</i>

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:06.760
<i>So keep on smiling</i>

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:10.720
<i>imasara tachidomarenu bokura no
nichijou jou</i>

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:10.720
<i>We're past the point of stopping
In our daily lives</i>

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:12.220
<i>michi joutou!</i>

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:12.220
<i>Bring on the unknown!</i>

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:14.560
<i>ano hi kimi to kabe ni kaita</i>

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:14.560
<i>That day, I drew on the wall with you</i>

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:17.190
<i>mikansei wo fukanzen wo</i>

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:17.190
<i>The incomplete, the imperfect</i>

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>imasara doko e mo ikenai ze tte</i>

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>"You can't go anywhere at this point"</i>

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:22.610
<i>aa sou kai nee! aa sou kai nee!</i>

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:22.610
<i>Oh, is that so?! Oh, is that so?!</i>

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:28.700
<i>nara otona ni nanka natcha ikenai nee</i>

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:28.700
<i>Then we don't want to become a grown-up</i>

00:22:31.330 --> 00:22:32.950
<i>The Digimon Encyclopedia!</i>

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:36.000
<i>Holydramon.</i>

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:38.920
<i>This Digimon mega evolves from Angewomon.</i>

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:38.960
LEVEL: MEGA

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:41.170
TYPE: HOLY DRAGON

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:42.380
<i>They say Holydramon is the one
who annihilates all evil.</i>

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:43.340
SPECIAL MOVE: HOLY FLAME

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:45.140
<i>Now, let's check this out!</i>

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:48.890
<i>The legendary Holydramon
only appears when fighting evil.</i>

00:22:48.890 --> 00:22:51.730
<i>Would Holydramon appear
if I did something bad?</i>

00:22:51.730 --> 00:22:55.100
<i>What if I painted stripes
on Tentomon's wings?</i>

00:22:57.640 --> 00:23:00.060
<i>Which Digimon will it be next time?</i>

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:05.070
<i>Sora and Garudamon are swallowed
into the boiling lava.</i>

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:08.580
<i>But that's when the wings
of miracles flutter.</i>

00:23:08.580 --> 00:23:12.080
<i>Next time on Digimon Adventure:
"Dance of the Heavens, Hououmon"</i>

00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:14.790
<i>The adventure continues to a new world.</i>
